{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Improve safeguarding and support for dementia care",
        "additional_details": "Also, the Government should:\r\n- Review the effectiveness of the legal obligation to provide a reference\r\n- work to ensure that, where there have been legitimate concerns about the suitability of an employee, these can be conveyed without fear of litigation or reprisal \r\n- Ensure all staff are trained in iatrogenic harm\r\n- make sure all dementia settings have mental health nurses present  \r\n- issue guidance making clear that a staff member's DBS check cannot be a guarantee of future behaviour.",
        "background": "The Government must appoint a Minister for Dementia Care, ensure all nurses are aware of their obligation to report harmful practice to the barring service and NMC, appoint a safeguarding nurse for every dementia care setting and mandate statutory CCTV in all dementia care settings.",
